Testing/Livewire/Filament gotchas (goldenland-realestate-v2): `aiAssistAdminUser()` / `propertyProviderFake()` register a `Gate::before` callback denying all other users — calling twice (or via nested `beforeEach` across describe blocks) registers two callbacks → AuthorizationException on the first `Gate::authorize`; call exactly once per test and keep shared `beforeEach` helpers idempotent. Filament action modals: the confirmation modal replaces the form step (it skips the form schema), so a custom action form must be the primary modal with warnings in the modal description; `callAction` leaves the action mounted → ActionNotResolvableException on a later `mountAction` — use a fresh component instance. The Filament test helper merges list state element-wise, so checkbox arrays need a direct `set`(statePath, value) instead of passing in `callAction` data; evidence state is set but not rendered server-side into modal HTML — assert on state, not HTML. Prefer the deterministic agents in tests to avoid network. <!-- created=2026-08-07, last=2026-08-07 -->
